# checks/emit-linked.sh (row P10.2): a leg's disagreement with native that
# was traced to a component outside the compiled path. One per line:
# <program> <leg> <reason>. The check reports these and does not fail on them.
#
# eval leg: the evaluator calls the core VALUE inc/dec, whose overflow is
# the value form's "integer overflow"; native compiles (inc x) as the IR op,
# "ExecutionError: integer overflow" once caught. The compiled leg calls the
# op form (wasm.eval/lk-inc, lk-dec) and matches native (2026-10-05).
corpus/opmatrix/inc.lg eval the core value inc lacks the op form's "ExecutionError: " overflow prefix
corpus/opmatrix/dec.lg eval the core value dec lacks the op form's "ExecutionError: " overflow prefix
